From d4cd4c9d1eec6b533ff0d2fb01c2a7a46bd893b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Jackson <70459+jjackson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:23:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Labs mode: act as an HQ mobile worker with an OAuth
 bearer token

Opt-in (formplayer.labs.enabled / LABS_ENABLED, off by default) mode for
connect-labs ("Connect Web") to drive formplayer as a CommCare mobile
worker without an HQ Django session or HQ's HMAC key.

- LabsAuthFilter: requests signed with X-Labs-Signature (Base64
  HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body, or the JSON part for multipart, keyed with
  formplayer.labs.authKey) and carrying X-Labs-HQ-Token authenticate as
  body username/domain. 401 on bad/missing signature or token,
  restoreAs, or a mixed HQ HMAC header. CSRF exempt (server-to-server).
- BearerTokenAuth: outbound restore/submit/case search send
  Authorization: Bearer <token>; never the HMAC branch, never `as=`.
- Labs submissions always go to /receiver/secure/ (the non-secure
  receiver ignores the bearer on domains without required auth).
- submit-all accepts meta_location (geopoint) and fills an empty
  meta/location: formplayer ignores <orx:pollsensor>, so Web Apps forms
  otherwise submit no GPS.
- sessionid cookie is optional on navigate_menu(_start), get_details,
  interval sync and incomplete-session routes (labs has no cookie).
- Token never logged (excluded from HqUserDetailsBean.toString).
- Dockerfile: Boot 3.3 launcher class is
  org.springframework.boot.loader.launch.JarLauncher; the old name made
  the image exit with ClassNotFoundException.
- docs/labs-mode.md: env vars, backing services, signing, API contract.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
