@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Labs mode (Connect Web)
+
+Labs mode lets the connect-labs backend drive formplayer as a CommCare **mobile worker**. It
+authenticates with the worker's **HQ OAuth2 bearer token** and does not use an HQ Django session or
+HQ's HMAC key. It is off by default. When it is off, formplayer behaves exactly as upstream.
+
+## Running
+
+| Env var | Property | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `LABS_ENABLED=true` | `formplayer.labs.enabled` | Turns labs mode on. Default `false`. |
+| `LABS_AUTH_KEY` | `formplayer.labs.authKey` | Shared secret with the labs backend. Required when enabled; startup fails if blank. |
+| `COMMCARE_HOST` | `commcarehq.host` | For example `https://www.commcarehq.org`. Restore, install and case-search URLs are built from it. |
+| `AUTH_KEY` | `commcarehq.formplayerAuthKey` | Still a required property. Labs never uses it, so set it to any random value unless HQ also calls this instance. |
+| `EXTERNAL_REQUEST_MODE` | `formplayer.externalRequestMode` | Leave empty in production. `replace-host` rewrites every outbound host to `COMMCARE_HOST` (dev or mocks only). |
+| `POSTGRESQL_HOST` / `_PORT` / `_DATABASE` / `_USERNAME` / `POSTGRESQL_PASSWROD` (sic) | `spring.datasource.*` | Postgres 10+ holds form/menu sessions, Flyway-migrated on boot. |
+| `REDIS_HOSTNAME` / `REDIS_PASSWORD` | `redis.*` | Redis holds locks, the CCZ archive index, sync and volatility caches. |
+| `SERVER_PORT` (8080) | `server.port` | API port. |
+| `MANAGEMENT_SERVER_PORT` (8081) | `management.server.port` | `GET /health` (db and redis), `/info`, `/metrics`. Keep it private. |
+| `sqlite.dataDir` (`dbs/`), `sqlite.tmpDataDir` (`tmp_dbs/`) | same | Local disk for per-user and per-app SQLite sandboxes, and the downloaded CCZs. Use a persistent volume; losing it only forces a reinstall and restore. |
+| `SENTRY_DSN`, datadog | optional | |
+
+Build and image: `./gradlew bootJar` (JDK 17) produces `build/libs/formplayer.jar`. Then
+`docker build .` builds the image. The Dockerfile copies the prebuilt jar and does not compile.
+
+## Authenticating a request
+
+Every request is a `POST` of JSON (`Content-Type: application/json`) with two headers:
+
+* `X-Labs-Signature`: standard padded Base64 of **HMAC-SHA256(key = LABS_AUTH_KEY, message =
+  the exact raw request body bytes)**. Sign the bytes you send, not a re-serialization. For the
+  multipart `answer_media` request, sign the bytes of the `application/json` part named `answer`.
+  The file part is not covered.
+* `X-Labs-HQ-Token`: the worker's HQ access token (scope `sync`) from HQ `/oauth/token/`. A
+  `Bearer ` prefix is optional. Send a fresh token on every request; formplayer never stores it.
+
+The body must contain `username` (the worker's short or full HQ username) and `domain`.
+`restoreAs` and `restoreAsCaseId` are rejected. A bad or missing signature, a missing token, a
+missing username or domain, or a request that also carries `X-MAC-DIGEST` gets **401** and the
+request stops there. No CSRF token or cookie is needed.
+
+```python
+body = json.dumps(payload).encode()
+sig = base64.b64encode(hmac.new(LABS_AUTH_KEY.encode(), body, hashlib.sha256).digest()).decode()
+requests.post(f"{FP}/navigate_menu", data=body, headers={
+    "Content-Type": "application/json", "X-Labs-Signature": sig, "X-Labs-HQ-Token": token})
+```
+
+Trust model: formplayer trusts the signed `username` and `domain` to name the token's own user.
+It does not cross-check them; HQ authorizes every outbound call by the token.
+
+What formplayer sends to HQ for a labs request:
+* `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on restore, submission, case search and remote instances. It
+  never sends HMAC or cookies.
+* The restore is a plain worker restore: `/a/<domain>/phone/restore/?version=2.0&device_id=…`, with
+  no `as=`.
+* Submissions go to the app profile's `PostURL`. In labs mode it is always rewritten to
+  `/receiver/secure/<build_id>/`, because the non-secure receiver ignores the bearer token on
+  domains that don't require auth.
+* The CCZ comes from `/a/<domain>/apps/api/download_ccz/?app_id=<app_id>&latest=save`. That HQ
+  endpoint is unauthenticated.
+
+## Which `app_id` to send
+
+Send the **released build id**, not Connect's `cc_app_id` (the master app id). Formplayer caches
+installs per `app_id` on disk and in Redis, so a master id would pin every user to whatever was
+installed first. With a build id, `latest=save` returns that exact build, which is how HQ Web
+Apps works.
+
+To resolve the build id, make an unauthenticated
+`GET <hq>/a/<domain>/apps/download/<cc_app_id>/media_profile.ccpr?latest=true`. This is Connect's
+install URL with `latest=true` added; on domains with per-location releases, also add
+`&username=<user>`. Then read the build id from the `PostURL` property
+(`…/receiver/secure/<build_id>/`). The profile's `version` attribute is the build version. When the
+version changes, call `update` (`{username, domain, app_id: <old build id>}`) or just start using
+the new build id.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+Every body includes `username` and `domain`. These fields are optional on any request:
+`tz_offset_millis`, `tz_from_browser` (IANA name), `windowWidth`, and `mustRestore`
+(force a sync first).
+
+| Endpoint | Extra fields | Response (brief) |
+|---|---|---|
+| `navigate_menu_start` | `app_id`, `locale`, `preview:false` | Root menu: `type:"commands"`, `commands[]` (`index`, `displayText`), `breadcrumbs`, `persistentMenu` |
+| `navigate_menu` | `app_id`, `selections[]` (menu indices / case ids, the full path from the root), `offset`, `search_text`, `sortIndex`, `cases_per_page`, `query_data`, `geo_location` (`"lat lon"`, used only for `here()` in case lists), `isShortDetail`, `selected_values` | A menu (`commands`), a case list (`type:"entities"`: `entities[]`, `headers`, `pageCount`, `currentPage`), a query screen, or, once a form opens, a **form**: `session_id`, `tree[]` (questions: `ix`, `caption`, `datatype`, `answer`, `choices`, `required`, `relevant`), `title`, `langs` |
+| `get_details` | `app_id`, `selections[]` ending in the case id, `isShortDetail` | `entityDetailList[]` (each has `title`, `headers`, `details` values) |
+| `answer` | `session_id`, `ix`, `answer`, optional `answersToValidate` | `status:"accepted"` or `"validation-error"`, `errors{ix: {status, type}}`, `tree[]` (whole form, updated) |
+| `answer_media` | multipart: `file` (the media) + `answer` (JSON part as for `answer`) | As `answer` |
+| `new-repeat` | `session_id`, `ix` (the repeat juncture) | `tree[]` |
+| `delete-repeat` | `session_id`, `ix` (the repeat instance) | `tree[]` |
+| `submit-all` | `session_id`, `answers{ix: answer}` (all answers), `prevalidated:true`, **`meta_location`** | See below |
+| `sync-db` | optional `preserveCache` | `{status:"accepted"}` after a restore from HQ |
+| `update` / `delete_application_dbs` | `app_id` | Clears that app install for the user |
+
+### Form GPS (`meta/location`)
+
+HQ forms with auto GPS capture contain `<cc:location/>` in `meta` and an `<orx:pollsensor>` action.
+Only commcare-android implements pollsensor; formplayer ignores it, so Web Apps submits an empty
+location. In labs mode, `submit-all` accepts `meta_location` as an XForms geopoint
+`"lat lon [altitude [accuracy]]"`, for example from `navigator.geolocation`:
+`"${latitude} ${longitude} ${altitude ?? 0} ${accuracy}"`. Formplayer writes it into an **empty**
+`meta/location` before serializing. A value already present is kept, and forms without the node
+are untouched. An invalid value returns `status:"error"` and nothing is sent to HQ. `geo_location`
+on navigation does **not** reach `meta/location`; it only feeds `here()`.
+
+### Submission results
+
+`submit-all` returns a `SubmitResponseBean`:
+* `status:"success"`. `submitResponseMessage` is HQ's OpenRosa `<message>` text. `nextScreen` is
+  the end-of-form navigation (a menu, a case list, or `null` for back to the start).
+* `status:"validation-error"`. `errors{ix: {...}}` covers answers that failed validation; nothing
+  was sent.
+* `status:"error"`. `notification.message` holds the reason. For an HQ 4xx it reads "Form
+  submission failed with error response: <status and HQ body>"; an HQ 5xx gives the exception
+  message. The local case DB is rolled back and the form session kept, so the same `submit-all`
+  can be retried.
+* `status:"too-many-requests"` (HQ 429) means retry later. `status:"case-cycle-error"` is a cyclic
+  case relationship.
+
+HQ answers synchronously. **Connect's processing is not synchronous**: Connect receives the form
+from HQ asynchronously, so learn progress, deliver units, flags and payments have to be read back
+from Connect afterwards. Match on the form's `meta/instanceID`.
